aluation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 2%).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 5% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of -8.8% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.2% (vs the 8% bar).","The 19 covering analysts target $44.24 on average, 9% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 6% falls short of the cost of capital of 5.7%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have been steady (CV 0.25).","It burns cash (FCF margin -25%).","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.36x.","ROE of 9% is amplified by 4.2x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","Operating margin is running 7pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 6.2x net debt to EBITDA ($548.0M of cash against $23.0B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 2.3x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 0.85 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD.","The current ratio of 0.91 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 0.1% over 3 years, 4.8% over 5 years and 2.4% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 16%).","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 5.5% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.01, a backlog worth 9% of annual revenue and deferred revenue down 4%.","Capex runs 3.2x depreciation (52.0% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.2%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only bought over the past year (1 purchase).","It returns 2.1% a year to shareholders (2.4% in dividends).","The share count has grown 0.8% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 64 consecutive years, raising it 7.9% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 8,794 employees, each generates about $1.1M of revenue, in line with the Utilities median.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$271K per employee.","CEO pay is $4.5M (4x revenue per employee)."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":26,"head":"Avoid: priced 74% above its fair value of $23.31.","pros":["Insiders net buyers ($41K over 12 months)"],"cons":["Trades 74% above fair value of $23.31","ROIC 5.5% vs WACC 5.7%","FCF margin 25.5% (burns cash)","Net debt/EBITDA 6.2x","Interest coverage only 2.3x"],"flags":["Priced 74% above its fair value of $23.31","Earns below its cost of capital and burns cash"],"need":[],"buy_below":19.81,"vc":{"base":23.31,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":23.31,"n_alt":2,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.0159,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":20.4014,"ev_ebitda":12.539,"pfcf":19.6541,"pb":1.8576,"roic":0.0568,"gross_margin":0.3591,"fcf_margin":-0.0633,"div_yield":0.0329}},"ticker":"CNP","date":"2026-11-06"}